# Sprint 1 — GREEN phase evidence (ledger-uniqueness)

target-feature-tests: PASS
regression-baseline: PASS

## Summary

Implementation:
- skills/_shared/lib/ledger.mjs: added `resolveEarnLedgerPath({ home, env })` (REQ-001) and
  `filterOwnWalletRows(rows, ownWallets)` (REQ-002), both pure/read-only, plus a REQ-005
  doc-comment documenting the two-ledger design at the top of the file.
- skills/earn/self-improve/lib/ledger_reader.py: added `filter_own_wallet_rows(rows, own_wallets)`
  (REQ-003 mirror of REQ-002) and a new opt-in `own_wallets=None` keyword parameter on both
  `realized_summary()` and `confirmed_net_series()` (REQ-003).

All target-feature tests now PASS:
- node --test skills/_shared/lib/__tests__/ledger-path.test.mjs -> 18/18 PASS.
- pytest tests/test_ledger_wallet_filter.py -> 14/14 PASS.

## Regression baseline (same scope declared in verification-architecture.md's Regression Gate)

- `node --test skills/_shared/lib/__tests__/ledger.test.js skills/_shared/lib/__tests__/ledger.test.mjs skills/_shared/lib/__tests__/ledger-path.test.mjs`
  -> 39/39 PASS (21 pre-existing + 18 new; zero pre-existing test changed behavior).
- `cd skills/earn/self-improve && python3 -m pytest tests/test_ledger_reader.py tests/test_ledger_resolution.py tests/test_realized_gate.py tests/test_ledger_wallet_filter.py -q`
  -> 54 passed, 3 failed (identical 3 pre-existing failures already documented and reproduced
  BEFORE any implementation code existed — see sprint-1-red-phase.log's "Regression baseline"
  section: 2 are a repo-wide `pm_backtest_strategy.py`/`conftest.patched_baseline_code` fixture
  drift unrelated to earn-ledger paths or wallets, reproduced on the pristine main checkout with
  zero changes from this feature; 1 is a worktree-path-literal assertion in a pre-existing test
  that fails identically for any worktree copy of this repo, not just this feature's). Pass
  count is UNCHANGED from the RED-phase regression baseline run (54 passed / 3 failed then too,
  before `filter_own_wallet_rows`/`own_wallets` existed) — proof this feature introduces zero
  new regressions.
- A wider `pytest tests/` (the full self-improve suite, beyond this feature's declared
  regression-gate scope) additionally shows 18 pre-existing failures, ALL sharing the exact
  same root cause (`conftest.py:37`, the same `edge_weight` fixture-drift assertion) across
  files this feature never touches (`test_adversary_disapprove.py`, `test_baseline_beat.py`,
  `test_denylist_reject.py`, `test_heldout_regress.py`, `test_risk_adjusted_fitness.py`) — a
  pre-existing, repo-wide `pm_backtest_strategy.py` fixture-drift issue, out of scope for
  ledger-uniqueness (not one of REQ-001..005's touched files) and not a regression this
  feature introduces.

